# Remote access: what to keep from the USB SSH work (draft revision)

**Draft, revised 2026-11-10.** It is meant to replace `remote-access.md` once the USB-networking session stops. Do
not build from it yet. Until then, `remote-access.md` and its `README.md` row stay as they are.

## Decision (owner, 2026-11-10)

**[debug-access.md](debug-access.md) is the only way to reach the phone from the Mac.** That means fshell over
`ECOMM.LDD` and a second CDC-ACM function, from Symbian's own tools, with no TCP/IP.

The USB SSH work (CDC-ECM Ethernet, smoltcp, Sunset SSH, `NEOSSH.EXE`) does not go into main. Its USB, power and
user-side improvements are useful for debug access, and are taken out of it below. The network and SSH parts are
parked.

## Status as found (2026-11-10)

From the session's own report (`remote-access.md`, "Phone results"):
- **D0–D5 pass in RAM boots:**
  - scp of 16 MiB at 2.67 MB/s up and 2.76 MB/s down, SHA-256 matching;
  - wrong-key refusal, interrupted transfer and resume, unplug and replug;
  - Mac sleep and wake, and a 5-minute stability run (21 of 21 logins).
- **D6 (installed cold boot) has not run.** Install images are prepared in `private/usbssh/install/`, but the
  installed slots haven't been written.

**Nothing is committed:**
- **kernel:** 5 modified files and 14 untracked ones;
- **`neolink`:** no commits at all;
- **`e32-rs`** and the docs changes: uncommitted.

## Review findings, rechecked

The 2026-11-09 findings, against the code as of 2026-11-10. `acm` = `sdm670_assp/qcom_dwc3_acm.cpp`.

| # | Finding | Now | Where |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Daemon exits on a full TX queue (`-9`) | fixed | `neossh/src/usb.rs:86` |
| 2 | A halt timeout aborts `Bringup` | changed on purpose: on failure USB stops and keeps its buffers, so DMA never reuses them | `acm:1281` |
| 3 | SET_INTERFACE clears the packet filter | open; harmless on macOS, which sets a filter | `acm:344` |
| 4 | A quarantined endpoint never recovers | fixed: a disconnect that needs it restarts the controller; replug passes | `acm:942` |
| 5 | The user can reach `C:\private\e0002010\` | open | `neossh/src/files.rs` |
| 6 | Weak Ed25519 authorized key accepted | open | — |
| 7 | Keepalive without a timeout | fixed: TCP keepalive every 10 s plus a peer timeout | `neolink/src/net.rs:53` |
| 8 | One session's error resets both | partly: a protocol error drops only its session; a storage-close error still resets both | `neolink/src/net.rs:177` |
| 9 | Throughput about 1.5 MB/s | fixed: 2.7 MB/s (activity boost) | — |
| 10 | Lower items | not rechecked | — |

Findings 3, 5, 6 and 8, and the ECM-only items of 10, are in parked code. Finding 2 and the DMA-barrier item of 10
come along with the kept USB core and are reviewed again when it lands.

## Keep: useful for debug access

| Piece | Files | What it gives debug access | Stage |
|---|---|---|---|
| Endpoint lifecycle, DMA ownership, EP0 recovery, controller restart | `acm` (core), `common/inc/a64_usb_dma.h`, `a64_usb_control.h` | a USB core that survives stalls, resets and replug | DA3, DA5 |
| Hot-traffic polling budget | `common/inc/a64_usb_poll.h` | latency under load | DA4 |
| Composite gadget and boot policy (the privileged ACM monitor stays hidden unless a development policy allows it) | `acm`, `common/inc/a64_usb_policy.h` | the second ACM function; who may reach the monitor | DA3, DA6 |
| Resume refresh (HS Suspend to On sends a fresh CONNECT/SPEED) | `common/inc/a64_usb_resume.h` | the link comes back after the Mac sleeps | DA5 |
| Activity boost (CPU idle clocks were the bottleneck: 0.66 to 2.67 MB/s) | `common/inc/a64_usb_activity.h` | ymodem and other transfers at full speed | DA4 |
| Cold-power wrapper-clock fix (`qcom,select-utmi-as-pipe-clk`; QSCRATCH changed from `0x0d` to `0x04`), tested with the monitor's `usb cold` (already in main, kernel `2692bea`) | `acm` (`Bringup`) | the first step of the normal-boot USB power fix | DA6, FS6 |
| Fixed-capacity frame FIFO | `common/inc/a64_usbnet_queue.h`, renamed `a64_usb_queue.h` | the ACM PDD's DFC bridge | DA3 |
| Host tests | `tools/test_usb_activity.cpp`, `test_usb_policy.cpp`, `test_usb_resume.cpp`, `test_usbnet_queue.cpp` | the kept logic stays tested | all |
| `e32` file and timer APIs: `File::read_at64`, `write_at64`, `set_size64`, `flush`, `set_att`, `set_modified`; `Fs::replace_file`, `read_dir_page`, `entry`; `Timer::wait_high_res`; the new neotest cases | `e32-rs/crates/e32/src/{fs,time}.rs`, `e32-sys`, `neotest` | general user-side APIs (Files, future Rust tools) | — |
| Mac acceptance method: hash-checked round trip, Unicode filename, interrupted transfer, 5-minute stability, sleep/wake | `private/usbssh/` (scripts and results) | the model for the DA4/DA5 exit tests in `phone.py` | DA4, DA5 |

## Park: not in main

Kept on a pushed kernel branch `usbnet-parked`, or in an archived repo.

| Piece | Files |
|---|---|
| ECM Ethernet | `common/inc/a64_usbnet.h` (HAL `ENeoHalUsbNetState/Rx/Tx`), `sdm670_assp/qcom_usbnet_descriptors.h`, the net TX/RX/filter/notification paths in `acm`, the `USBNET` switch in `variant.conf`, `a64_variant.cpp` and `build/neo` |
| Hardware random numbers | `sdm670_assp/qcom_prng.cpp`, HAL `0x4e23`, `A64StartPrng`, its mapping in `pixel_bonito.cpp`, the PRNG clock hook in `qcom_mss.cpp` (reviewed safe for telephony) |
| SSH and SFTP | `neolink` as a whole (smoltcp, Sunset, SFTP, shell, `NEOSSH.EXE`): pushed as `NeoSymbian/neolink` and archived, or a bundle listed in `retired-repos.md` |

## How to split

Done by the session that owns the code, or by the owner, once that session stops:

1. **Save everything:** commit the kernel work as it is to `usbnet-parked` and push it, so nothing is lost.
2. **Kernel main:** a commit with only the "Keep" rows, built without `USBNET`. It must boot on QEMU and on bonito with
   the monitor working (`phone.py cmd log`, `dump`, `shot`, `usb cold`). Then re-pin `build/sources.lock`.
3. **`e32-rs`:** a commit of the file and timer APIs and their tests.
4. **`neolink`:** push and archive it.
5. **Docs:** promote this draft over `remote-access.md`, and point the `README.md` row to `debug-access.md`.

## If remote access returns

For example SSH over Wi-Fi, or ECM again:
- start from `usbnet-parked` and `neolink`;
- fix findings 5, 6 and 8 first;
- add ECM as a third USB function beside the two ACM functions of debug access;
- D6 shares the normal-boot USB power fix with debug access DA6 and FS6.
